<article class="env-lemma" id="06J4">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06J4">Lemma <span data-tag="06J4">9.4.4.15</span>.</a> Let $\lambda $ be an uncountable regular cardinal, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a $\lambda $-small simplicial set, and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a left fibration of simplicial sets. Assume that $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is weakly contractible. Then there is a weakly contractible $\lambda $-small subset $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ such that $U|_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' }$ is also a left fibration. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $K$ and $L$ are subsets of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, let us write $K \Subset L$ if $K$ is contained in $L$ and the following addition conditions are satisfied: 
    <p>
<dl>
<dt>$(a)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For $0 \leq i &lt; n$, every lifting problem 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \Lambda ^{n}_{i} \ar [r]^-{\sigma _0} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{ U } \\ \Delta ^ n \ar [r] \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{\sigma } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \]
</div>
<p>
 having the property that $\sigma _0$ factors through $K$ admits a solution, where the $n$-simplex $\sigma $ is contained in $L$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(b)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every finite simplicial subset $K_0 \subseteq K$, the composite map $K_0 \hookrightarrow L \hookrightarrow \operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(L)$ is nullhomotopic. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<p>
       If $K$ is $\lambda $-small, then the collection of finite simplicial subsets $K_0 \subseteq K$ and the collection of all lifting problems of the above form are both $\lambda $-small. We can then use our assumptions that $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is weakly contractible and that $U$ is a left fibration to choose a $\lambda $-small subset $L \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ satisfying $K \Subset L$. Applying this observation repeatedly, we can choose a sequence of $\lambda $-small sets 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \emptyset = K(0) \Subset K(1) \Subset K(2) \Subset K(3) \Subset \cdots  \]
</div>
<p>
       The union $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' = \bigcup _{n \geq 0} K(n)$ then has the desired properties. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></p></p></article>
